2. Third-party files not covered by the Apache-2.0 grant

   paper/Definitions/ holds the MDPI LaTeX template (MDPI_template_ACS.zip, downloaded by the
   author from mdpi.com on 2026-09-28; mdpi.cls declares version v6.5a dated 2026-09-11;
   paper/TEMPLATE.md records the source and the sha256 of each file). The files are kept only to
   build the manuscript and stay under their owners' terms. No file states a licence for
   itself.

   - mdpi.cls, mdpi.bst, journalnames.tex, unicode.tex: the MDPI template. mdpi.cls gives
     latex@mdpi.com as its contact.
   - mdpi_apacite.sty, mdpi_apacite.bst: derived from the apacite package ("Copyright (C)
     1994-2013 Erik Meijer and any individual authors listed elsewhere in this file"),
     modified by MDPI.
   - mdpi_chicago.bst: the chicago.bst style by Glenn Paulley (version 4, 1992, as its header
     states).
   - logo-mdpi.eps, logo-updates.eps, logo-orcid.pdf: logo files supplied with the template.

3. Programs and libraries that are not in this repository

   The systems and libraries that the benchmarks run against (OpenSSL, nghttp2, nginx, HAProxy,
   Envoy, Caddy with caddy-l4, sslh, Netty, Jetty, cmux and hyper-util) are downloaded from the
   release URLs and hashes pinned in bench/cmake/pins.cmake, or from the registries named in the
   lock files under bench/competitors. They are not part of this repository and keep their own
   licences.
